<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.11.3: Reasoning Symbolically and Abstractly about Linear Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00244</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.11.3: Reasoning Symbolically and Abstractly about Linear Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4a21ca3e-11e7-4b29-b12e-40fb195885ba</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>For numbers 1 – 5, select the slope and intercept that corresponds to each equation:</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="6c21e788-9cde-4e5b-94cc-e15e1e947b3f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\( -4x+3y=3 \)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="290e6cf0-44ff-4e9c-88f4-1105c2b6945d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\( 12x-4y=8 \)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="dc16004d-1b6c-4990-830a-3a35112e31e5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\( 8x+2y=16 \)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="85f7342e-2dc9-4623-b35e-32e5737b516d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\( -x+\frac 13 y=\frac 13 \)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\( m=3, y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! ( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="4f72d334-bc7f-4d5d-bf3e-1696a83110e9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\( -4x + 3y = -6 \)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
            <para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <para>
        <emphasis>Using Standard Form and Intercepts to Graph</emphasis>
      </para>
      <para> Standard form, \(Ax + By = C\), is helpful for finding the \(x\)-intercepts and \(y\)-intercepts of an equation. </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="d693b658-f7c3-4288-9f1b-0baf9a491166" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 6 - 11,</para>
            <para>
              <quote>Use the equation \(6x -4y=24\).</quote>
            </para>
            <para>What is the value of \(y\) at the \(x\)-intercept?</para>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="8bab532e-ecf3-48f9-a6e5-4505f13ce64e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para>What is the \(x\)-intercept of the equation?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 4</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="04605dc6-d8fc-45b1-a167-4208032018fe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para>What is the value of \(x\) at the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="59849d8c-16fa-497f-85ed-a7fc1d68615a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
            <para>What is the \(y\)-intercept of the equation?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! -6</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is -6.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
