      <exercise class="RFM1">
        <problem>
          <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
          <para>For numbers 1-2, use the equations below:</para>
          <para>
            <quote>These are the equations from the activity. Each equation is in the form \(Ax+By=C\)</quote>
          </para>
          <para>\( 4x - 3y = -3 \)
      \( 12x - 4y = 8 \)
      \( 8x + 2y = 16 \)
      \( 3x - y = -1\)
      \( 4x - 3y = 6 \)
    </para>
          <para>Observe the graph of the equation \(−4x+3y=3\) where it is graphed, on the same coordinate plane, with another line passing through \((0,0)\) and \((A,B)\). In this example \(A=-4\) and \(B=3\), so the other line would pass through \((0,0)\) and \((−4,3)\). What do you notice about the lines?
      </para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Answers may vary, but here is a sample.The two lines are perpendicular.
    </para>
          <para>
            <figure>
              <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_13_06_02.jpg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
          </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
